<!--
  Fast DDS profile for the control PC (multi-homed: 2 arms, camera link, lab, docker).

  PURPOSE 1 - stop camera black-holing:
    Restrict the PC's UDP transport to loopback + the 10G camera link (192.168.10.100)
    so the PC does NOT advertise docker0 (172.17.0.1) etc. The Jetson also owns a
    docker0 172.17.0.1 and mis-routes image data to its own bridge otherwise
    (topics visible, `ros2 topic hz` stale). interfaceWhiteList requires
    useBuiltinTransports=false to take effect.

  PURPOSE 2 - keep DISCOVERY working for the whole robot graph:
    useBuiltinTransports=false ALSO removes Fast DDS's automatic multicast discovery.
    We cannot re-add multicast here: in this Fast DDS (2.6) a custom
    metatrafficMulticastLocatorList + initialPeersList together break discovery
    entirely (0 peers), and the lab switch does not reliably pass multicast anyway.
    So discovery is pure UNICAST: we enumerate the well-known metatraffic-unicast
    ports of the first N same-host participants, and the same ports on the Jetson.

    Metatraffic unicast port = 7400 + 250*ROS_DOMAIN_ID + 10 + 2*participantId.
    This workspace uses ROS_DOMAIN_ID=5  ->  base 8660, i.e. 8660 + 2*participantId.
    The list below covers participantId 0..39 (up to 40 local participants).
    IF YOU CHANGE ROS_DOMAIN_ID OR RUN >40 LOCAL NODES, REGENERATE THESE PORTS,
    or discovery will silently island the later participants (that failure is what
    took down the whole franka_right side before this fix).

  Verified: 18/18 local participants discover each other on domain 5 (default-DDS
  parity). Counterpart on the Jetson: /home/toelle/fastdds_jetson.xml.
  Longer-term cleaner options (remove this hack): Fast DDS Discovery Server, or an
  IGMP querier / disable IGMP-snooping on the switch so multicast survives.
-->
<profiles xmlns="http://www.eprosima.com/XMLSchemas/fastRTPS_Profiles">
    <transport_descriptors>
        <transport_descriptor>
            <transport_id>udp_transport</transport_id>
            <type>UDPv4</type>
            <interfaceWhiteList>
                <address>127.0.0.1</address>
                <address>192.168.10.100</address>
            </interfaceWhiteList>
            <sendBufferSize>134217728</sendBufferSize>
            <receiveBufferSize>134217728</receiveBufferSize>
        </transport_descriptor>
    </transport_descriptors>

    <participant profile_name="pc_participant" is_default_profile="true">
